  "planted": "R14c changed what the hunt sends before the judge's probes (lag probed first, with a filler event between a refusal and the decision that reads it, then a consistency replay and a conformance suite to depth 4), so a planted trial runs more and other sessions and fewer profiles explain them all: every planted difference is the same reported class with fewer profiles in it (no trial changed class, all 96 stay right); R14d only meters the same sessions (a bundled simulated engine is admitted without a scope), so it changes none.",
  "stranger": "R14c's hunt sends other sessions to a stranger (lag first, the conformance suite), and a stranger's residual is the number of sessions no best-fitting profile explains, so it moves with what was sent (every stranger still has a residual and no reported profile); R14d's ceilings are never reached by a bundled engine and change nothing here."
